    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25420" root="ضأن" body-key="D">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضِئْنِىٌّ</span></b>  is an extr., distorted, rel. n. [from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَأْنٌ</span>].
(M.) You say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِعْزًى ضِئْنِيَّةٌ</span> <i>Goats that keep to
the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَأْن</span> [or <i>sheep</i>]. (M.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِقَآءٌ ضِئْنِىٌّ</span> <i>A
wide,</i> (M,) or <i>large,</i> (K,) <i>skin, of the hide of a
sheep,</i> (M, K,) <i>in which</i> [<i>milk such as is termed</i>]
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَائِب</span> <i>is churned.</i> (K.)

